<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sineus</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sineus is one of the three Varangian brothers who, according to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/primary-chronicle">Russian Primary Chronicle</a>, were invited by the Slavic and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/finnic-peoples">Finnic peoples</a> of the north in 862 to rule over them. While <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rurik">Rurik</a> settled at Novgorod and Truvor at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/izborsk">Izborsk</a>, Sineus is said to have taken Beloozero, dying two years later. Most historians regard Sineus and Truvor as legendary figures.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sineus.jpg" alt="Sineus" width="320" height="226" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Viktor Vasnetsov · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Prizvanievaryagov.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
